# Unreal Engine generated directories
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/

# Build/ follows Epic's own pattern rather than a bare "Build/".
# A bare ignore drops files that must be tracked once the project has branding or
# platform packaging: Build/Windows/Resources/*.ico, Application.manifest, and
# Build/*/PakBlacklist*.txt. Ignore the contents, keep the directory structure
# traversable, then un-ignore what is genuinely source. (CORE-001, B-1.)
Build/*
!Build/*/
Build/*/**
!Build/*/Resources/
!Build/*/Resources/**
!Build/*/*.manifest
!Build/*/PakBlacklist*.txt
Intermediate/
Saved/
Platforms/*/Binaries/
Platforms/*/Build/
Platforms/*/Intermediate/

# Plugin-local generated directories
Plugins/**/Binaries/
Plugins/**/Intermediate/

# IDE / tooling
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sln
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
# Anchored to the repository root. Unanchored, these would drop a legitimately
# vendored third-party CMakeLists.txt or Makefile under Source/ThirdParty. (CORE-001, B-1.)
/CMakeLists.txt
/Makefile
/compile_commands.json

# Build artifacts.
# Anchored to generated locations rather than ignored at any depth. Unanchored,
# a future Source/ThirdParty/**/x64/*.lib would be silently dropped while its
# sibling *.dll commits via .gitattributes LFS tracking -- producing a repo that
# links on the author's machine and nowhere else. (CORE-001, B-1.)
# *.obj is anchored, and must stay anchored. It is both an MSVC object file and
# Wavefront OBJ, the most common mesh interchange format. Unanchored, it silently
# drops Source/Art/**/*.obj and Content/Raw/**/*.obj -- an original source mesh that
# never commits is an asset whose provenance cannot be demonstrated later, while the
# author's own clone looks fine. That collides directly with the ledger requirement
# in CLAUDE.md and PROMPT_TO_START.md. (CORE-001, NEW-1.)
Intermediate/**/*.obj
Binaries/**/*.obj

# Compiler-only extensions with no content-side meaning. Safe at any depth.
*.ipdb
*.iobj
*.exp
*.ilk

# Belt-and-braces. These cannot match today -- Binaries/, Intermediate/ and
# Plugins/**/Binaries/ are excluded wholesale above and git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so *.pdb/*.lib there are already ignored by those lines. Kept
# so the intent survives if a parent exclusion is ever narrowed. Do not treat them as
# load-bearing. (CORE-001, NEW-2.)
Binaries/**/*.pdb
Binaries/**/*.lib
Intermediate/**/*.pdb
Intermediate/**/*.lib
Plugins/**/Binaries/**/*.pdb
Plugins/**/Binaries/**/*.lib

# Packaged / staged output
Packaged/

# Generated by the engine, not vendored by us.
# PixelStreaming2RTC.Build.cs:152-153 declares these as RuntimeDependencies and
# copies them from $(PluginDir)/Resources/WebServers into $(ProjectDir)/Samples
# at build time, overwriting whatever is there. Tracking them means tracking
# build output that the next build rewrites. See ASSET-0006.
Samples/PixelStreaming2/WebServers/
Archive/
StagedBuilds/

# Pixel Streaming Infrastructure is fetched and pinned, never vendored.
# See Docs/Environment.md for the pinned branch and commit.
Web/PixelStreamingInfrastructure/
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Unreal MCP generated client config: machine-local, loopback-only, never shared.
.mcp.json

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
